      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 9.533,
       "text": "Swap a and b: a moving drops D(a), b moving drops D(b).",
       "sceneId": "a01-why2w"
      },
      {
       "start": 9.533,
       "end": 17.444,
       "text": "But both count the a–b edge as “fixed”, and it still crosses after the swap: 2w too many.",
       "sceneId": "a01-why2w"
      },
      {
       "start": 17.444,
       "end": 24.467,
       "text": "E↔D: 9 − 10 = −1; counting the cut directly, 12 → 13, it agrees.",
       "sceneId": "a01-why2w"
      },
      {
       "start": 24.867,
       "end": 30.333,
       "text": "An eight-node graph from an alternating seed: cut 7.",
       "sceneId": "a02-negative"
      },
      {
       "start": 30.333,
       "end": 33.578,
       "text": "The best first step is only −1.",
       "sceneId": "a02-negative"
      },
      {
       "start": 33.578,
       "end": 38.378,
       "text": "But step two is +7: keep two steps, cut 1.",
       "sceneId": "a02-negative"
      },
      {
       "start": 38.378,
       "end": 43.622,
       "text": "A greedy that accepts only gains would stop at 7 right away.",
       "sceneId": "a02-negative"
      },
      {
       "start": 44.022,
       "end": 50.156,
       "text": "Why must a prefix be consecutive? Each gain depends on the steps before it.",
       "sceneId": "a03-prefix"
      },
      {
       "start": 50.156,
       "end": 56.956,
       "text": "Pass 2's D↔B is +2 in sequence, but −12 alone from the start.",
       "sceneId": "a03-prefix"
      },
      {
       "start": 56.956,
       "end": 61.156,
       "text": "So take only the first k steps; k = 0 is valid too.",
       "sceneId": "a03-prefix"
      },
      {
       "start": 61.556,
       "end": 65.689,
       "text": "Change the seed: three seeds reach cut 3.",
       "sceneId": "a04-seed"
      },
      {
       "start": 65.689,
       "end": 70.933,
       "text": "But AB | CDE stays at 5: both trials lose.",
       "sceneId": "a04-seed"
      },
      {
       "start": 70.933,
       "end": 76.622,
       "text": "Reaching DE | ABC needs two pairs at once: a local optimum.",
       "sceneId": "a04-seed"
      },
      {
       "start": 77.022,
       "end": 80.489,
       "text": "Give A area 3 and the rest 1.",
       "sceneId": "a05-area"
      },
      {
       "start": 80.489,
       "end": 86.844,
       "text": "After A↔D the count is still 2 to 3, but the area goes from 4 : 3 to 2 : 5.",
       "sceneId": "a05-area"
      },
      {
       "start": 86.844,
       "end": 91.2,
       "text": "KL keeps only the count; area needs its own check.",
       "sceneId": "a05-area"
      },
      {
       "start": 91.6,
       "end": 94.178,
       "text": "A pass has n/2 steps.",
       "sceneId": "a06-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 94.178,
       "end": 97.867,
       "text": "Each step looks at up to (n/2)² pairs.",
       "sceneId": "a06-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 97.867,
       "end": 103.333,
       "text": "A naive pass is about n³; sorting by D prunes a lot.",
       "sceneId": "a06-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 103.333,
       "end": 108.8,
       "text": "Next module's FM moves one node at a time, for a near-linear pass.",
       "sceneId": "a06-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 109.2,
       "end": 111.267,
       "text": "Six things to keep.",
       "sceneId": "a07-summary"
      },
      {
       "start": 124.267,
       "end": 128.178,
       "text": "Next: move one node at a time.",
       "sceneId": "a07-summary"
      }
